infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title setNoDelay(true) vs Nagle on (default)
  desc Same small-write protocol — flush each write now for latency, or coalesce for throughput
  compares
    - label setNoDelay(true): Nagle off
      children
        - label Each write() goes out immediately
          desc Disables Nagle's hold-small-segments batching
        - label No ~40 ms delayed-ACK stall
          desc Removes the Nagle + delayed-ACK round-trip stall
        - label Right for RPC, REPL, games
          desc Low latency on small, interactive messages
        - label More, smaller packets on the wire
          desc You give up coalescing's per-packet savings
    - label Default: Nagle on
      children
        - label Small writes coalesced into packets
          desc Holds a small segment until ACK or a full packet
        - label ~40 ms stall per round trip
          desc Small request/response waits on the peer's delayed ACK
        - label Right for bulk throughput
          desc Many tiny writes batch into fewer sends
        - label Fewer packets, less overhead
          desc Coalescing cuts per-packet network cost
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f59e0b
